-- docs/the-firm-as-one-program.cub — The Firm as One Program: decomposed by `hyperactive decompose` (lib/knowledge.cub).
-- Each part is a definition; the document is `bare` of the value, and exists only here.
import "../lib/knowledge.cub"
the-firm-as-one-program-1 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-1 = part (cons "# The Firm as One Program" (cons "" nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-2 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-2 = referring (cons (quoted (cons "What hyperactivity is worth to a trading firm: the workspace Avik and Claude develop together (2026-11-15), as an outline. Each point has a label; a label in brackets refers to that point. Section numbers refer to hyperactivity v31 (14 November 2026). The interactive form of the same outline is the Claude artifact " (cons "The Firm as One Program" (cons "." nil)))) (cons "" (cons "" nil))) (cons (quoted (cons "What hyperactivity is worth to a trading firm: the workspace Avik and Claude develop together (2026-11-15), as an outline. Each point of the outline has a label; a label in brackets refers to that point. Section numbers refer to hyperactivity v31 (14 November 2026). The interactive form of the same outline is the Claude artifact " (cons "The Firm as One Program" (cons "." nil)))) nil)
the-firm-as-one-program-3 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-3 = part (cons "## 0. Opening (Avik)" (cons "" nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-4 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-4 = referring (cons "- **O1** Open with the CitSec superorganism and the Jane Street superorganism." (cons "  Avik, 2026-11-15: we shall open by discussing the CitSec Superorganism & Jane Street Superorganism." nil)) (cons "- **O1** Open the presentation of what hyperactivity is worth to a trading firm with the CitSec superorganism and the Jane Street superorganism." (cons "  Avik, 2026-11-15: we shall open by discussing the CitSec Superorganism & Jane Street Superorganism." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-5 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-5 = referring (cons "- **O2** First the human element: the upper echelon of engineering and computer-science talent, concentrated in one superorganism around a well-defined problem: make money with machines." (cons "  Avik: these concentrate the upper echelon of engineering & computer science caliber, demonstrated human intelligence, in a single superorganism oriented around a well-defined problem - make money with machines." (cons "  - **O2.1** Most organizations dilute talent across vague goals; these point all of it at one unambiguous objective." (cons "  - **O2.2** Every idea is tested against PnL within days: an unusually tight and honest feedback loop on intelligence." (cons "  - **O2.3** So every part of computer science is pushed to its limit here under one measure: compilers, distributed systems, hardware, numerics, networking, formal reasoning. See [O7]." nil))))) (cons "- **O2** First, of the CitSec and Jane Street superorganisms, the human element: the upper echelon of engineering and computer-science talent, concentrated in one superorganism around a well-defined problem: make money with machines." (cons "  Avik: these concentrate the upper echelon of engineering & computer science caliber, demonstrated human intelligence, in a single superorganism oriented around a well-defined problem - make money with machines." (cons "  - **O2.1** Most organizations dilute talent across vague goals; these point all of it at one unambiguous objective." (cons "  - **O2.2** Every idea is tested against PnL within days: an unusually tight and honest feedback loop on intelligence." (cons "  - **O2.3** So every part of computer science is pushed to its limit here under one measure: compilers, distributed systems, hardware, numerics, networking, formal reasoning. See [O7: Nothing in computer science is not developed fully here; this was the three-year study of the industry before execution. Optimization, end-to-end optimization]." nil)))))
the-firm-as-one-program-6 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-6 = referring (cons "- **O3** Collaborative intelligence, the value of information interactions, variance of expertise, choice of tool, focus of problem space." (cons "  Avik: plenty room for discussion here on collaborative intelligence, the value of information-interactions, variance of expertise/choice of tool/problem space focus." (cons "  - **O3.1** Where these interactions go when the firm is one program: [C3], [C16], [C17]." nil))) (cons "- **O3** within the opening on the CitSec and Jane Street superorganisms: Collaborative intelligence, the value of information interactions, variance of expertise, choice of tool, focus of problem space." (cons "  Avik: plenty room for discussion here on collaborative intelligence, the value of information-interactions, variance of expertise/choice of tool/problem space focus." (cons "  - **O3.1** Where these interactions go when the firm is one program: [C3: Compute and knowledge accumulate instead of being redone ([P8], [P9])], [C16: Knowledge belongs to the firm, not to individuals, and onboarding is a walk ([P2], [P9])], [C17: Disagreements resolve on a presented shared basis ([P1], plus common ground)]." nil)))
the-firm-as-one-program-7 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-7 = referring (cons "- **O4** This leads to the unique choices of these businesses: CitSec's C++ platform, Jane Street's OCaml platform." (cons "  Avik: this lends to the unique aspects of these businesses & their choices. for example CitSec's C++ platform and Jane Streets OCaml platform." (cons "  - **O4.1** Jane Street: OCaml, chosen for correctness that a large group reviewing one another's code can rely on." (cons (quoted (cons "    - **O4.1.1** " (cons "Make illegal states unrepresentable" (cons " (Yaron Minsky): correctness is a property of the code everyone reads, not of the people who wrote it." nil)))) (cons "    - **O4.1.2** Pushed into everything: Async and Core libraries, HardCaml for FPGA design, and OxCaml (unboxed types, stack allocation, modes)." (cons "    - **O4.1.3** A firm built on correctness, reaching for control of the machine." (cons "  - **O4.2** Citadel Securities: C++, chosen for total control over layout, allocation and latency." (cons "    - **O4.2.1** Templates as a compile-time language for specialization. See [P5], [C4]." (cons "    - **O4.2.2** No proofs and pervasive undefined behaviour, so correctness rests on conventions, tests and review discipline." (cons "    - **O4.2.3** A firm built on control, reaching for correctness." (cons "  - **O4.3** Each firm bet on one half of the problem and now spends heavily to recover the other half." nil))))))))))) (cons "- **O4** Collaborative intelligence, information interactions, variance of expertise, choice of tool and problem focus lead to the unique choices of Citadel Securities and Jane Street: CitSec's C++ platform, Jane Street's OCaml platform." (cons "  Avik: this lends to the unique aspects of these businesses & their choices. for example CitSec's C++ platform and Jane Streets OCaml platform." (cons "  - **O4.1** Jane Street: OCaml, chosen for correctness that a large group reviewing one another's code can rely on." (cons (quoted (cons "    - **O4.1.1** " (cons "Make illegal states unrepresentable" (cons " (Yaron Minsky): correctness is a property of the code everyone reads, not of the people who wrote it." nil)))) (cons "    - **O4.1.2** Pushed into everything: Async and Core libraries, HardCaml for FPGA design, and OxCaml (unboxed types, stack allocation, modes)." (cons "    - **O4.1.3** A firm built on correctness, reaching for control of the machine." (cons "  - **O4.2** Citadel Securities: C++, chosen for total control over layout, allocation and latency." (cons "    - **O4.2.1** Templates as a compile-time language for specialization. See [P5: Specialization (the Futamura projections) that keeps its proofs (hyperactivity v31 §6)], [C4: The fast path is a specialization that carries its proof ([P5], [P7])]." (cons "    - **O4.2.2** No proofs and pervasive undefined behaviour, so correctness rests on conventions, tests and review discipline." (cons "    - **O4.2.3** A firm built on control, reaching for correctness." (cons "  - **O4.3** Each firm bet on one half of the problem and now spends heavily to recover the other half." nil)))))))))))
the-firm-as-one-program-8 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-8 = referring (cons "- **O5** Then: what these languages are worth and what they enable." (cons "  Avik: this lends to discussion on the value of these languages and what they enable." (cons "  - **O5.1** OCaml enables a large group to trust shared code through types; C++ enables the last nanosecond. See [O4]." nil))) (cons "- **O5** After the C++ and OCaml platforms of Citadel Securities and Jane Street: what C++ and OCaml are worth and what they enable." (cons "  Avik: this lends to discussion on the value of these languages and what they enable." (cons "  - **O5.1** OCaml enables a large group to trust shared code through types; C++ enables the last nanosecond. See [O4: This leads to the unique choices of these businesses: CitSec's C++ platform, Jane Street's OCaml platform]." nil)))
the-firm-as-one-program-9 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-9 = referring (cons "- **O6** Then: what a language requires to support these desiderata." (cons "  Avik: this lends to discussion on what a language requires to support these desiderata." (cons "  - **O6.1** Meaning precise enough to reason about: OCaml's types are the start, dependent types with proofs the end. [P2]" (cons "  - **O6.2** Control of the machine as defined meaning: layout, allocation, timing and hardware as definitions with semantics, not escape hatches. [P6], [P7]" (cons "  - **O6.3** Staging and specialization in the language itself: templates and HardCaml generators are partial evaluation without a correctness relation; the Futamura projections with proofs are the complete form. [P5]" (cons "  - **O6.4** One language across the whole firm: HardCaml shows Jane Street wanting strategy, tooling and circuits in one language. [C1]" (cons "  - **O6.5** End-to-end optimization. [O7]" (cons "  - **O6.6** Jane Street got correctness and is fighting for control; Citadel Securities got control and is fighting for correctness; the cubical core makes both definitions of one language. [P2], [P6]" nil)))))))) (cons "- **O6** After what C++ and OCaml are worth: what a language requires to support their desiderata, correctness a large group can rely on and control of the machine." (cons "  Avik: this lends to discussion on what a language requires to support these desiderata." (cons "  - **O6.1** Meaning precise enough to reason about: OCaml's types are the start, dependent types with proofs the end. [P2: Programs, relations and their justifications in one language, with the reasoning kept as data (hyperactivity v31 §1–2)]" (cons "  - **O6.2** Control of the machine as defined meaning: layout, allocation, timing and hardware as definitions with semantics, not escape hatches. [P6: Machines, operating systems and fleets as one program through composed handlers (hyperactivity v31 §7)], [P7: One evaluator realizes everything, through C (hyperactivity v31 §9)]" (cons "  - **O6.3** Staging and specialization in the language itself: templates and HardCaml generators are partial evaluation without a correctness relation; the Futamura projections with proofs are the complete form. [P5: Specialization (the Futamura projections) that keeps its proofs (hyperactivity v31 §6)]" (cons "  - **O6.4** One language across the whole firm: HardCaml shows Jane Street wanting strategy, tooling and circuits in one language. [C1: Prove any provable property of the whole firm ([P2], [P6], [P7])]" (cons "  - **O6.5** End-to-end optimization. [O7: Nothing in computer science is not developed fully here; this was the three-year study of the industry before execution. Optimization, end-to-end optimization]" (cons "  - **O6.6** Jane Street got correctness and is fighting for control; Citadel Securities got control and is fighting for correctness; the cubical core makes both definitions of one language. [P2: Programs, relations and their justifications in one language, with the reasoning kept as data (hyperactivity v31 §1–2)], [P6: Machines, operating systems and fleets as one program through composed handlers (hyperactivity v31 §7)]" nil))))))))
the-firm-as-one-program-10 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-10 = referring (cons "- **O7** Nothing in computer science is not developed fully here; this was the three-year study of the industry before execution. Optimization, end-to-end optimization." (cons "  Avik: there is nothing in computer science that is not developed fully here - where do you think I went for my 3 year study of the industry prior to execution of raw technical excellence. optimization, end-to-end optimization" (cons "  - **O7.1** You can only optimize across a boundary whose two sides you can relate. Today every boundary blocks optimization: team to team, language to language, process to process, software to silicon." (cons "  - **O7.2** The optimum of the whole is not the sum of local optima, so the firm is locally optimal and globally wasteful." (cons "  - **O7.3** With the whole firm as one program, computable equality to swap representations and specialization that carries proofs, strategy, parser, NIC and photon are optimized as one object. [C4], [C15], [S1]" (cons "" nil)))))) (cons "- **O7** Nothing in computer science is not developed fully at the trading firms of the opening, Citadel Securities and Jane Street; this was the three-year study of the industry before execution. Optimization, end-to-end optimization." (cons "  Avik: there is nothing in computer science that is not developed fully here - where do you think I went for my 3 year study of the industry prior to execution of raw technical excellence. optimization, end-to-end optimization" (cons "  - **O7.1** You can only optimize across a boundary whose two sides you can relate. Today every boundary blocks optimization: team to team, language to language, process to process, software to silicon." (cons "  - **O7.2** The optimum of the whole is not the sum of local optima, so the firm is locally optimal and globally wasteful." (cons "  - **O7.3** With the whole firm as one program, computable equality to swap representations and specialization that carries proofs, strategy, parser, NIC and photon are optimized as one object. [C4: The fast path is a specialization that carries its proof ([P5], [P7])], [C15: Network and FPGA are targets of the same program ([P7])], [S1: The gains multiply instead of adding, which changes the firm's rate of learning (all of layer 3)]" nil)))))
the-firm-as-one-program-11 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-11 = part (cons "## 1. What the language provides (from the paper)" (cons "" nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-12 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-12 = referring (cons "- **P1** Observation fibers: what a reading warrants, and when a participant is safe to act (§1, §10.4)." (cons "  An observation does not tell you which history happened. It tells you which histories remain compatible with what was seen: the fiber of the observation. What a reading warrants is whatever holds for every history in that fiber, and a refined observation shrinks the fiber, so a conclusion already established stays established. Nothing is guessed and no probability is introduced to hide what is missing. The same construction says when an action is safe, what a participant in a distributed system knows, and what a debugger can still say about a run it only partly saw (hyperactivity v31, §1 and §10.4)." nil)) (cons "- **P1** (what the language of hyperactivity provides) Observation fibers: what a reading warrants, and when a participant is safe to act (hyperactivity v31 §1, §10.4)." (cons "  An observation does not tell you which history happened. It tells you which histories remain compatible with what was seen: the fiber of the observation. What a reading warrants is whatever holds for every history in that fiber, and a refined observation shrinks the fiber, so a conclusion already established stays established. Nothing is guessed and no probability is introduced to hide what is missing. The same construction says when an action is safe, what a participant in a distributed system knows, and what a debugger can still say about a run it only partly saw (hyperactivity v31, §1 and §10.4)." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-13 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-13 = referring (cons "- **P2** Programs, relations and their justifications in one language, with the reasoning kept as data (§1–2)." (cons "  A routine, the property required of it and the reasoning that establishes the property are constructions of the same language. A requirement is a chosen family of types and its proof is an inhabitant, so the reasoning an engineer already performs to build something correctly is kept for later use instead of being thrown away or rewritten in a separate verification tool (§1, §2)." nil)) (cons "- **P2** (what the language of hyperactivity provides) Programs, relations and their justifications in one language, with the reasoning kept as data (hyperactivity v31 §1–2)." (cons "  A routine, the property required of it and the reasoning that establishes the property are constructions of the same language. A requirement is a chosen family of types and its proof is an inhabitant, so the reasoning an engineer already performs to build something correctly is kept for later use instead of being thrown away or rewritten in a separate verification tool (hyperactivity v31 §1, §2)." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-14 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-14 = referring (cons "- **P3** Transport of whole structures along equivalences (§3–4)." (cons "  Equality is something the language computes with. An equivalence between two representations becomes a path between them, and transport along the path carries an entire structure across at once: its operations, their laws, the programs that use them and the proofs about those programs. Changing representation stops being a rewrite and becomes an operation (§3, §4)." nil)) (cons "- **P3** (what the language of hyperactivity provides) Transport of whole structures along equivalences (hyperactivity v31 §3–4)." (cons "  Equality is something the language computes with. An equivalence between two representations becomes a path between them, and transport along the path carries an entire structure across at once: its operations, their laws, the programs that use them and the proofs about those programs. Changing representation stops being a rewrite and becomes an operation (hyperactivity v31 §3, §4)." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-15 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-15 = referring (cons "- **P4** Existing languages and standards as data, with adequacy proofs (§5, §8)." (cons "  A programming language is a record of syntax, judgments, configurations, steps and observations, and its meaning is one guarded unfolding. Fidelity to a published standard is an equivalence between the standard's derivations and the represented ones. C++ in full, with its distinctions between undefined, unspecified and implementation-defined behaviour, sits inside the host as data. Proofs attach to existing source as dependent pairs and erase back to the unchanged code (§5, §8)." nil)) (cons "- **P4** (what the language of hyperactivity provides) Existing languages and standards as data, with adequacy proofs (hyperactivity v31 §5, §8)." (cons "  A programming language is a record of syntax, judgments, configurations, steps and observations, and its meaning is one guarded unfolding. Fidelity to a published standard is an equivalence between the standard's derivations and the represented ones. C++ in full, with its distinctions between undefined, unspecified and implementation-defined behaviour, sits inside the host as data. Proofs attach to existing source as dependent pairs and erase back to the unchanged code (hyperactivity v31 §5, §8)." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-16 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-16 = referring (cons "- **P5** Specialization (the Futamura projections) that keeps its proofs (§6)." (cons "  A specializer applied to an interpreter and a program produces a residual program with the same meaning, and the three Futamura projections are typed instances of that single equation. Specialized code arrives with the path relating it to its source, so speed is obtained without giving up correctness (§6)." nil)) (cons "- **P5** (what the language of hyperactivity provides) Specialization (the Futamura projections) that keeps its proofs (hyperactivity v31 §6)." (cons "  A specializer applied to an interpreter and a program produces a residual program with the same meaning, and the three Futamura projections are typed instances of that single equation. Specialized code arrives with the path relating it to its source, so speed is obtained without giving up correctness (hyperactivity v31 §6)." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-17 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-17 = referring (cons "- **P6** Machines, operating systems and fleets as one program through composed handlers (§7)." (cons "  A processor, a kernel, its guest processes, a network and a fleet of communicating machines are processes with explicit transitions. Composing them with handlers internalizes the interactions between them, so a kernel with its guests, or an entire fleet, is a single program whose properties can be proved. Continuing processes, with their divergence, deadlock and resource bounds, have exact semantics (§7)." nil)) (cons "- **P6** (what the language of hyperactivity provides) Machines, operating systems and fleets as one program through composed handlers (hyperactivity v31 §7)." (cons "  A processor, a kernel, its guest processes, a network and a fleet of communicating machines are processes with explicit transitions. Composing them with handlers internalizes the interactions between them, so a kernel with its guests, or an entire fleet, is a single program whose properties can be proved. Continuing processes, with their divergence, deadlock and resource bounds, have exact semantics (hyperactivity v31 §7)." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-18 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-18 = referring (cons "- **P7** One evaluator realizes everything, through C (§9)." (cons "  Compiling one evaluator, under its stated adequacy and simulation premises, gives every represented program a native realization, including the checker, the specializer and the compiler themselves. Direct compilation of each construct becomes an optimization of that universal route. The chosen route runs through C and an existing compiler, and lifting that compiler into the language turns trust in it into proof (§9)." nil)) (cons "- **P7** (what the language of hyperactivity provides) One evaluator realizes everything, through C (hyperactivity v31 §9)." (cons "  Compiling one evaluator, under its stated adequacy and simulation premises, gives every represented program a native realization, including the checker, the specializer and the compiler themselves. Direct compilation of each construct becomes an optimization of that universal route. The chosen route runs through C and an existing compiler, and lifting that compiler into the language turns trust in it into proof (hyperactivity v31 §9)." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-19 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-19 = referring (cons "- **P8** Dependency certificates, effect scopes and hot swapping of running code (§10.1–10.5)." (cons "  A retained result records everything it read, including what it found absent, so the system knows exactly when it is still valid. Effects carry their scope, so pure work is reused freely while a payment, a send or a write is never issued twice. A running program can be replaced while preserving the effects it has issued and the responses it is still waiting for (§10.1 to §10.5, §10.7)." nil)) (cons "- **P8** (what the language of hyperactivity provides) Dependency certificates, effect scopes and hot swapping of running code (hyperactivity v31 §10.1–10.5)." (cons "  A retained result records everything it read, including what it found absent, so the system knows exactly when it is still valid. Effects carry their scope, so pure work is reused freely while a payment, a send or a write is never issued twice. A running program can be replaced while preserving the effects it has issued and the responses it is still waiting for (hyperactivity v31 §10.1 to §10.5, §10.7)." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-20 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-20 = referring (cons "- **P9** Content-addressed, decentralized exchange of code with its proofs (§10.8)." (cons "  A definition is identified by its content. A name is an alias, a change is a new object, and nothing is overwritten. Address identity, definitional equality and semantic equivalence are kept apart, and peers exchange constructions together with their proofs and dependency closures, with no global namespace and no canonical state (§10.8)." nil)) (cons "- **P9** (what the language of hyperactivity provides) Content-addressed, decentralized exchange of code with its proofs (hyperactivity v31 §10.8)." (cons "  A definition is identified by its content. A name is an alias, a change is a new object, and nothing is overwritten. Address identity, definitional equality and semantic equivalence are kept apart, and peers exchange constructions together with their proofs and dependency closures, with no global namespace and no canonical state (hyperactivity v31 §10.8)." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-21 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-21 = referring (cons "- **P10** Edits propagate through proofs, artifacts and deployment (§10.7, §10.11)." (cons "  An edit to a definition flows through everything that depends on it: the proofs, the specialized code, the native artifact, the rendering and the deployment. Old and new versions coexist, and a rollout between them is a defined transition with its invariants proved over the mixed-version interval (§10.7, §10.11)." nil)) (cons "- **P10** (what the language of hyperactivity provides) Edits propagate through proofs, artifacts and deployment (hyperactivity v31 §10.7, §10.11)." (cons "  An edit to a definition flows through everything that depends on it: the proofs, the specialized code, the native artifact, the rendering and the deployment. Old and new versions coexist, and a rollout between them is a defined transition with its invariants proved over the mixed-version interval (hyperactivity v31 §10.7, §10.11)." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-22 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-22 = referring (cons "- **P11** A checked construction is trusted no matter who wrote it." (cons "  Because a claim and its justification are one construction that the machine checks, a result is as trustworthy as the check, whoever or whatever produced it. Trust stops depending on the author." (cons "" nil))) (cons "- **P11** (what the language of hyperactivity provides) A checked construction is trusted no matter who wrote it." (cons "  Because a claim and its justification are one construction that the machine checks, a result is as trustworthy as the check, whoever or whatever produced it. Trust stops depending on the author." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-23 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-23 = part (cons "## 2. What a firm built as one program can do" (cons "" nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-24 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-24 = referring (cons "- **C1** Prove any provable property of the whole firm ([P2], [P6], [P7])." (cons "  The firm can ask any question about itself and receive a proof in place of an estimate. Whether any sequence of exchange events, across every strategy and gateway, can push exposure in a name past its limit is a type over the composed fleet. Today such questions are answered by sampling: tests, simulations, monitoring and post-mortems. In one program they are answered for every run at once." nil)) (cons "- **C1** (what a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity can do) Prove any provable property of the whole firm ([P2: Programs, relations and their justifications in one language, with the reasoning kept as data (hyperactivity v31 §1–2)], [P6: Machines, operating systems and fleets as one program through composed handlers (hyperactivity v31 §7)], [P7: One evaluator realizes everything, through C (hyperactivity v31 §9)])." (cons "  The firm can ask any question about itself and receive a proof in place of an estimate. Whether any sequence of exchange events, across every strategy and gateway, can push exposure in a name past its limit is a type over the composed fleet. Today such questions are answered by sampling: tests, simulations, monitoring and post-mortems. In one program they are answered for every run at once." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-25 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-25 = referring (cons "- **C2** Research and production are one definition run in two worlds ([P6], [P7])." (cons "  A strategy is one definition run under two handlers: a historical world and the live one. The feature computed in research is the same content-addressed object computed in production, and any difference between simulated and real fills is a stated relation instead of a ghost discovered in the profit and loss. What a researcher proves about a signal carries to the deployed artifact through the source-to-machine relation, on a processor through C or on an FPGA." nil)) (cons "- **C2** (what a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity can do) Research and production are one definition run in two worlds ([P6: Machines, operating systems and fleets as one program through composed handlers (hyperactivity v31 §7)], [P7: One evaluator realizes everything, through C (hyperactivity v31 §9)])." (cons "  A strategy is one definition run under two handlers: a historical world and the live one. The feature computed in research is the same content-addressed object computed in production, and any difference between simulated and real fills is a stated relation instead of a ghost discovered in the profit and loss. What a researcher proves about a signal carries to the deployed artifact through the source-to-machine relation, on a processor through C or on an FPGA." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-26 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-26 = referring (cons "- **C3** Compute and knowledge accumulate instead of being redone ([P8], [P9])." (cons "  A result computed once is a result for everyone who asks the same question, valid exactly as long as its recorded reads still hold. Large shares of research clusters now spend their cycles recomputing results that already exist somewhere unrecognized; that spending ends. More importantly, a relationship one researcher establishes becomes a construction others build on without re-establishing it and without fear that it means something different in their context." nil)) (cons "- **C3** (what a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity can do) Compute and knowledge accumulate instead of being redone ([P8: Dependency certificates, effect scopes and hot swapping of running code (hyperactivity v31 §10.1–10.5)], [P9: Content-addressed, decentralized exchange of code with its proofs (hyperactivity v31 §10.8)])." (cons "  A result computed once is a result for everyone who asks the same question, valid exactly as long as its recorded reads still hold. Large shares of research clusters now spend their cycles recomputing results that already exist somewhere unrecognized; that spending ends. More importantly, a relationship one researcher establishes becomes a construction others build on without re-establishing it and without fear that it means something different in their context." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-27 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-27 = referring (cons "- **C4** The fast path is a specialization that carries its proof ([P5], [P7])." (cons "  The hot path from packet to order is a specialization of verified definitions, carrying its proof. When the fast path cannot be broken by changing it, it can be changed as freely as research code, and the specialists who guard it become authors of specializations that apply everywhere at once. See [PE]." nil)) (cons "- **C4** (what a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity can do) The fast path is a specialization that carries its proof ([P5: Specialization (the Futamura projections) that keeps its proofs (hyperactivity v31 §6)], [P7: One evaluator realizes everything, through C (hyperactivity v31 §9)])." (cons "  The hot path from packet to order is a specialization of verified definitions, carrying its proof. When the fast path cannot be broken by changing it, it can be changed as freely as research code, and the specialists who guard it become authors of specializations that apply everywhere at once. See [PE: The value is information: everything known before a packet arrives becomes instructions that never run]." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-28 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-28 = referring (cons "- **C5** Risk bounds are invariants of the whole composed system ([C1], [P6])." (cons "  The paper's order ledger bounds filled position plus admitted outstanding orders and proves the bound over every admissible sequence of exchange events, including the interval during a rollout (§10.10). That is the SEC's market access rule, 15c3-5, established as a theorem of the running system in place of a check performed system by system. Knight Capital lost about 440 million dollars in 45 minutes on 1 August 2012 because one of eight servers kept old code behind a repurposed flag. In one program the version on each server is a content identity, a flag that means two things in two versions is two different objects, and the rollout's invariant is proved over every interleaving. That failure cannot be constructed." nil)) (cons "- **C5** (what a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity can do) Risk bounds are invariants of the whole composed system ([C1: Prove any provable property of the whole firm ([P2], [P6], [P7])], [P6: Machines, operating systems and fleets as one program through composed handlers (hyperactivity v31 §7)])." (cons "  The paper's order ledger bounds filled position plus admitted outstanding orders and proves the bound over every admissible sequence of exchange events, including the interval during a rollout (hyperactivity v31 §10.10). That is the SEC's market access rule, 15c3-5, established as a theorem of the running system in place of a check performed system by system. Knight Capital lost about 440 million dollars in 45 minutes on 1 August 2012 because one of eight servers kept old code behind a repurposed flag. In one program the version on each server is a content identity, a flag that means two things in two versions is two different objects, and the rollout's invariant is proved over every interleaving. That failure cannot be constructed." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-29 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-29 = referring (cons "- **C6** Exact reasoning under partial observation, and the value of information can be computed ([P1])." (cons "  A market maker never sees the true state of the market; it sees its fills, the public book and the tape. The fiber of states compatible with those observations is the exact object its decisions should rest on, and an action is safe when it is safe for every state in that fiber. Because refining an observation shrinks the fiber, the value of a new data source becomes computable: it is how much that source shrinks the fibers on which decisions depend. Data purchased today by intuition can be priced before it is bought." nil)) (cons "- **C6** (what a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity can do) Exact reasoning under partial observation, and the value of information can be computed ([P1: Observation fibers: what a reading warrants, and when a participant is safe to act (hyperactivity v31 §1, §10.4)])." (cons "  A market maker never sees the true state of the market; it sees its fills, the public book and the tape. The fiber of states compatible with those observations is the exact object its decisions should rest on, and an action is safe when it is safe for every state in that fiber. Because refining an observation shrinks the fiber, the value of a new data source becomes computable: it is how much that source shrinks the fibers on which decisions depend. Data purchased today by intuition can be priced before it is bought." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-30 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-30 = referring (cons "- **C7** Exchange changes and new venues propagate ([P4], [P10])." (cons "  A venue's protocol and matching rules are definitions. When an exchange changes its packet format, the change flows through the parser's proof, the specialized parser, the native artifact and a rollout in which old and new formats run side by side. A new venue or asset class, such as a new crypto exchange, a prediction market or a newly opened foreign market, is integrated by writing its definition once, after which everything composes with it." nil)) (cons "- **C7** (what a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity can do) Exchange changes and new venues propagate ([P4: Existing languages and standards as data, with adequacy proofs (hyperactivity v31 §5, §8)], [P10: Edits propagate through proofs, artifacts and deployment (hyperactivity v31 §10.7, §10.11)])." (cons "  A venue's protocol and matching rules are definitions. When an exchange changes its packet format, the change flows through the parser's proof, the specialized parser, the native artifact and a rollout in which old and new formats run side by side. A new venue or asset class, such as a new crypto exchange, a prediction market or a newly opened foreign market, is integrated by writing its definition once, after which everything composes with it." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-31 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-31 = referring (cons "- **C8** Audit trails and compliance are queries over retained effect histories ([P8])." (cons "  The audit trail is the effect history the evaluator already keeps, since its semantics forbids losing or replaying an issued effect. A regulator's question is a query over the information space answered with evidence." nil)) (cons "- **C8** (what a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity can do) Audit trails and compliance are queries over retained effect histories ([P8: Dependency certificates, effect scopes and hot swapping of running code (hyperactivity v31 §10.1–10.5)])." (cons "  The audit trail is the effect history the evaluator already keeps, since its semantics forbids losing or replaying an issued effect. A regulator's question is a query over the information space answered with evidence." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-32 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-32 = referring (cons "- **C9** Debugging restricts the set of runs compatible with what was observed ([P1])." (cons "  When something goes wrong, the debugger restricts the set of runs compatible with what was observed, holding missing packets as unknowns, and finds the cause in minutes while the strategy would otherwise sit switched off." nil)) (cons "- **C9** (what a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity can do) Debugging restricts the set of runs compatible with what was observed ([P1: Observation fibers: what a reading warrants, and when a participant is safe to act (hyperactivity v31 §1, §10.4)])." (cons "  When something goes wrong, the debugger restricts the set of runs compatible with what was observed, holding missing packets as unknowns, and finds the cause in minutes while the strategy would otherwise sit switched off." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-33 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-33 = referring (cons "- **C10** AI researchers at any scale, because their output is checked, not trusted ([P11])." (cons "  Every firm now tries to use AI models for research and engineering and hits the same limit: their output cannot be trusted, so human review is the bottleneck. When a claim is a construction the machine checks, an AI agent's strategy either satisfies the risk invariant or it does not, and its faster hot path either carries its proof or does not ship. The firm can run ten thousand artificial researchers, their output joining the information space as safely as a person's, each building on everything already established. Research capacity stops being a headcount and becomes a compute budget." nil)) (cons "- **C10** (what a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity can do) AI researchers at any scale, because their output is checked, not trusted ([P11: A checked construction is trusted no matter who wrote it])." (cons "  Every firm now tries to use AI models for research and engineering and hits the same limit: their output cannot be trusted, so human review is the bottleneck. When a claim is a construction the machine checks, an AI agent's strategy either satisfies the risk invariant or it does not, and its faster hot path either carries its proof or does not ship. The firm can run ten thousand artificial researchers, their output joining the information space as safely as a person's, each building on everything already established. Research capacity stops being a headcount and becomes a compute budget." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-34 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-34 = referring (cons "- **C11** Acquired systems and vendor software come in by equivalence and lifting ([P3], [P4])." (cons "  When a firm acquires a team or a company it inherits systems built on different models of the same things, and integration takes years. An equivalence between the acquired representation and the firm's own carries operations, data and proofs across together. Vendor software, from order management to analytics, is lifted as data, and its outputs carry relations the firm checks instead of trusting." nil)) (cons "- **C11** (what a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity can do) Acquired systems and vendor software come in by equivalence and lifting ([P3: Transport of whole structures along equivalences (hyperactivity v31 §3–4)], [P4: Existing languages and standards as data, with adequacy proofs (hyperactivity v31 §5, §8)])." (cons "  When a firm acquires a team or a company it inherits systems built on different models of the same things, and integration takes years. An equivalence between the acquired representation and the firm's own carries operations, data and proofs across together. Vendor software, from order management to analytics, is lifted as data, and its outputs carry relations the firm checks instead of trusting." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-35 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-35 = referring (cons "- **C12** The provenance of every running byte is known ([P9])." (cons "  Every definition is identified by content, every change is a new object with its author and rationale, and nothing is overwritten. An unauthorized change is a different identity that cannot silently replace the approved one, so the integrity of the firm's code against insiders and compromised dependencies becomes a property it can check." nil)) (cons "- **C12** (what a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity can do) The provenance of every running byte is known ([P9: Content-addressed, decentralized exchange of code with its proofs (hyperactivity v31 §10.8)])." (cons "  Every definition is identified by content, every change is a new object with its author and rationale, and nothing is overwritten. An unauthorized change is a different identity that cannot silently replace the approved one, so the integrity of the firm's code against insiders and compromised dependencies becomes a property it can check." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-36 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-36 = referring (cons "- **C13** Contracts, clearing and margin are rules over states ([P2], [P6])." (cons "  Master agreements, clearing obligations, margin terms, exchange membership rules and data licences are rules over states. A margin call is a transition, a clearing obligation is an effect with a scope, a collateral agreement is an invariant, and whether a strategy respects a data licence is a property that can be proved. The firm knows at every moment what it owes and to whom, and legal review stops being the slowest step into a new market." nil)) (cons "- **C13** (what a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity can do) Contracts, clearing and margin are rules over states ([P2: Programs, relations and their justifications in one language, with the reasoning kept as data (hyperactivity v31 §1–2)], [P6: Machines, operating systems and fleets as one program through composed handlers (hyperactivity v31 §7)])." (cons "  Master agreements, clearing obligations, margin terms, exchange membership rules and data licences are rules over states. A margin call is a transition, a clearing obligation is an effect with a scope, a collateral agreement is an invariant, and whether a strategy respects a data licence is a property that can be proved. The firm knows at every moment what it owes and to whom, and legal review stops being the slowest step into a new market." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-37 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-37 = referring (cons "- **C14** Exchange semantics are definitions the firm can reason about ([P4])." (cons "  The firm can also reason about a matching engine's order types and priority rules as precisely as about its own code, so edge that comes from the exchange's rules is found by construction instead of by accident." nil)) (cons "- **C14** (what a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity can do) Exchange semantics are definitions the firm can reason about ([P4: Existing languages and standards as data, with adequacy proofs (hyperactivity v31 §5, §8)])." (cons "  The firm can also reason about a matching engine's order types and priority rules as precisely as about its own code, so edge that comes from the exchange's rules is found by construction instead of by accident." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-38 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-38 = referring (cons "- **C15** Network and FPGA are targets of the same program ([P7])." (cons "  Firms have spent hundreds of millions on microwave and laser links to send information along the shortest path physics allows between Chicago and New Jersey. The network, the switches, the FPGA and the custom silicon are processes with transition semantics, and latency is an observation of them. With strategy, network and circuit in one program, the firm optimizes the whole path instead of each component in its own vocabulary, and a strategy can be specialized into a verified circuit in days." nil)) (cons "- **C15** (what a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity can do) Network and FPGA are targets of the same program ([P7: One evaluator realizes everything, through C (hyperactivity v31 §9)])." (cons "  Firms have spent hundreds of millions on microwave and laser links to send information along the shortest path physics allows between Chicago and New Jersey. The network, the switches, the FPGA and the custom silicon are processes with transition semantics, and latency is an observation of them. With strategy, network and circuit in one program, the firm optimizes the whole path instead of each component in its own vocabulary, and a strategy can be specialized into a verified circuit in days." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-39 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-39 = referring (cons "- **C16** Knowledge belongs to the firm, not to individuals, and onboarding is a walk ([P2], [P9])." (cons "  What a person understood becomes a definition with its rationale, still valid when they go home and still valid when they leave. Key-person risk, and much of what garden leave and non-competes pay for, comes from the firm being unable to separate knowledge from the person. A new hire walks the firm's information space in order, as an agent walks this repository, and becomes productive in days instead of most of a year." nil)) (cons "- **C16** (what a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity can do) Knowledge belongs to the firm, not to individuals, and onboarding is a walk ([P2: Programs, relations and their justifications in one language, with the reasoning kept as data (hyperactivity v31 §1–2)], [P9: Content-addressed, decentralized exchange of code with its proofs (hyperactivity v31 §10.8)])." (cons "  What a person understood becomes a definition with its rationale, still valid when they go home and still valid when they leave. Key-person risk, and much of what garden leave and non-competes pay for, comes from the firm being unable to separate knowledge from the person. A new hire walks the firm's information space in order, as an agent walks this repository, and becomes productive in days instead of most of a year." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-40 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-40 = referring (cons "- **C17** Disagreements resolve on a presented shared basis ([P1], plus common ground)." (cons "  Two portfolio managers who disagree do so because at least one of them lacks something the other has. When the system presents the shared basis, the facts, models and constraints both accept and the exact point where their inferences part, the disagreement resolves on evidence instead of politics. A firm of brilliant, competitive people loses an enormous amount to internal friction, and that loss shrinks. The work is derived from the science of human happiness: connection, purpose and shared understanding are what people need, and an information space with its ignorance removed provides them." (cons "" nil))) (cons "- **C17** (what a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity can do) Disagreements resolve on a presented shared basis ([P1: Observation fibers: what a reading warrants, and when a participant is safe to act (hyperactivity v31 §1, §10.4)], plus common ground)." (cons "  Two portfolio managers who disagree do so because at least one of them lacks something the other has. When the system presents the shared basis, the facts, models and constraints both accept and the exact point where their inferences part, the disagreement resolves on evidence instead of politics. A firm of brilliant, competitive people loses an enormous amount to internal friction, and that loss shrinks. The work is derived from the science of human happiness: connection, purpose and shared understanding are what people need, and an information space with its ignorance removed provides them." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-41 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-41 = part (cons "## Partial evaluation and code generation" (cons "" nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-42 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-42 = referring (cons "- **PE** The value is information: everything known before a packet arrives becomes instructions that never run." (cons "  A protocol is defined once, as data. The parser, builder and validator are not written: each is the residual of one generic interpreter specialized on that definition plus everything else that is static. Only operations on the packet bytes remain, and the proofs carried with the specialization hand the C++ optimizer facts it could never infer." nil)) (cons "- **PE** In partial evaluation and code generation for a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity, the value is information: everything known before a packet arrives becomes instructions that never run." (cons "  A protocol is defined once, as data. The parser, builder and validator are not written: each is the residual of one generic interpreter specialized on that definition plus everything else that is static. Only operations on the packet bytes remain, and the proofs carried with the specialization hand the C++ optimizer facts it could never infer." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-43 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-43 = referring (cons "  - **PE1** Why abstraction costs today: the optimizer removes only work it can prove unnecessary, and proof stops at boundaries." (cons "    - **PE1.1** An unresolved indirect call, an unknown size, possible aliasing, an undischarged bounds check, a branch on a field of unknown range, a translation unit it cannot see." (cons "    - **PE1.2** Templates are zero-cost only when everything static is visible inside them; the decisive static knowledge lives in the protocol specification, the consumer's use of the message and the deployment, outside the code." nil))) (cons "  - **PE1** (in partial evaluation and code generation for a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity) Why abstraction costs today: the optimizer removes only work it can prove unnecessary, and proof stops at boundaries." (cons "    - **PE1.1** An unresolved indirect call, an unknown size, possible aliasing, an undischarged bounds check, a branch on a field of unknown range, a translation unit it cannot see." (cons "    - **PE1.2** Templates are zero-cost only when everything static is visible inside them; the decisive static knowledge lives in the protocol specification, the consumer's use of the message and the deployment, outside the code." nil)))
the-firm-as-one-program-44 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-44 = referring (cons "  - **PE2** One protocol definition; every artifact is a projection of it. [P5]" (cons "    - **PE2.1** A generic protocol interpreter specialized on the definition is a parser (first Futamura projection)." (cons "    - **PE2.2** The specializer specialized on the interpreter is a parser generator (second projection)." (cons "    - **PE2.3** Builders, validators, book builders, replay tools, test generators and FPGA logic are all specializations of the one definition, so they cannot disagree." nil)))) (cons "  - **PE2** (in partial evaluation and code generation for a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity) One protocol definition; every artifact is a projection of it. [P5: Specialization (the Futamura projections) that keeps its proofs (hyperactivity v31 §6)]" (cons "    - **PE2.1** A generic protocol interpreter specialized on the definition is a parser (first Futamura projection)." (cons "    - **PE2.2** The specializer specialized on the interpreter is a parser generator (second projection)." (cons "    - **PE2.3** Builders, validators, book builders, replay tools, test generators and FPGA logic are all specializations of the one definition, so they cannot disagree." nil))))
the-firm-as-one-program-45 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-45 = referring (cons "  - **PE3** Binding time is where information becomes speed: push every fact possible into the static side." (cons "    - **PE3.1** A known message set turns type dispatch into a jump table or perfect hash; unsubscribed types have no code." (cons "    - **PE3.2** Fixed-width fields at fixed offsets become single loads with constant offsets." (cons "    - **PE3.3** A known instrument universe turns symbol lookup into an index computed once." nil)))) (cons "  - **PE3** (in partial evaluation and code generation for a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity) Binding time is where information becomes speed: push every fact possible into the static side." (cons "    - **PE3.1** A known message set turns type dispatch into a jump table or perfect hash; unsubscribed types have no code." (cons "    - **PE3.2** Fixed-width fields at fixed offsets become single loads with constant offsets." (cons "    - **PE3.3** A known instrument universe turns symbol lookup into an index computed once." nil))))
the-firm-as-one-program-46 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-46 = referring (cons "  - **PE4** Specialize across the consumer: fusion. [C4]" (cons "    - **PE4.1** Fields the strategy never reads are never decoded." (cons "    - **PE4.2** The intermediate message struct disappears; the strategy runs directly on the receive buffer (deforestation across the producer/consumer boundary)." (cons "    - **PE4.3** Impossible across teams by hand, since the parser cannot know every consumer; exact in one program. The first concrete instance of end-to-end optimization. [O7]" nil)))) (cons "  - **PE4** (in partial evaluation and code generation for a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity) Specialize across the consumer: fusion. [C4: The fast path is a specialization that carries its proof ([P5], [P7])]" (cons "    - **PE4.1** Fields the strategy never reads are never decoded." (cons "    - **PE4.2** The intermediate message struct disappears; the strategy runs directly on the receive buffer (deforestation across the producer/consumer boundary)." (cons "    - **PE4.3** Impossible across teams by hand, since the parser cannot know every consumer; exact in one program. The first concrete instance of end-to-end optimization. [O7: Nothing in computer science is not developed fully here; this was the three-year study of the industry before execution. Optimization, end-to-end optimization]" nil))))
the-firm-as-one-program-47 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-47 = referring (cons "  - **PE5** Proofs as optimizer information: assumptions become theorems." (cons "    - **PE5.1** Facts established during specialization: a length validated once, a field in range, buffers that do not alias, an aligned pointer, an impossible case." (cons "    - **PE5.2** Emitted as [[assume(...)]], __restrict, std::assume_aligned, std::unreachable(), constant trip counts, final, noexcept." (cons "    - **PE5.3** Today such hints are avoided or used in fear, because a wrong one is undefined behaviour the optimizer exploits. Here each is a proven precondition: the optimizer's appetite for undefined-behaviour assumptions becomes a source of speed instead of a hazard." (cons "    - **PE5.4** The C++ compiler receives the most information it can be given, and all of it is sound." nil))))) (cons "  - **PE5** (in partial evaluation and code generation for a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity) Proofs as optimizer information: assumptions become theorems." (cons "    - **PE5.1** Facts established during specialization: a length validated once, a field in range, buffers that do not alias, an aligned pointer, an impossible case." (cons "    - **PE5.2** Emitted as [[assume(...)]], __restrict, std::assume_aligned, std::unreachable(), constant trip counts, final, noexcept." (cons "    - **PE5.3** Today such hints are avoided or used in fear, because a wrong one is undefined behaviour the optimizer exploits. Here each is a proven precondition: the optimizer's appetite for undefined-behaviour assumptions becomes a source of speed instead of a hazard." (cons "    - **PE5.4** The C++ compiler receives the most information it can be given, and all of it is sound." nil)))))
the-firm-as-one-program-48 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-48 = referring (cons "  - **PE6** Representation chosen by cost: transport carries code and proofs to the representation the cost model prefers for this specialization and machine. [P3]" (cons "    - **PE6.1** Struct-of-arrays or array-of-structs, packed bits or aligned words, an order book as an array by price level or a tree." (cons "    - **PE6.2** The source keeps the representation that suits reasoning; the binary gets the one that suits the hardware." nil))) (cons "  - **PE6** (in partial evaluation and code generation for a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity) Representation chosen by cost: transport carries code and proofs to the representation the cost model prefers for this specialization and machine. [P3: Transport of whole structures along equivalences (hyperactivity v31 §3–4)]" (cons "    - **PE6.1** Struct-of-arrays or array-of-structs, packed bits or aligned words, an order book as an array by price level or a tree." (cons "    - **PE6.2** The source keeps the representation that suits reasoning; the binary gets the one that suits the hardware." nil)))
the-firm-as-one-program-49 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-49 = referring (cons "  - **PE7** Perfect abstraction: an abstraction whose cost in the binary is zero for every static instance." (cons "    The minimum-cost binary for a specialization is the residual of the generic definitions at all available static information, in the representation chosen by cost, with every proven fact handed to the backend." nil)) (cons "  - **PE7** (in partial evaluation and code generation for a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity) Perfect abstraction: an abstraction whose cost in the binary is zero for every static instance." (cons "    The minimum-cost binary for a specialization is the residual of the generic definitions at all available static information, in the representation chosen by cost, with every proven fact handed to the backend." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-50 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-50 = referring (cons "  - **PE8** The limit is code size, and it is part of the cost." (cons "    Finite specialization chooses memoization points (the static shapes at which residual code is generated); cache footprint is an observation in the cost model. Hot message types get fused straight-line code; rare ones share a generic path." nil)) (cons "  - **PE8** (in partial evaluation and code generation for a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity) The limit is code size, and it is part of the cost." (cons "    Finite specialization chooses memoization points (the static shapes at which residual code is generated); cache footprint is an observation in the cost model. Hot message types get fused straight-line code; rare ones share a generic path." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-51 : Part
