the-firm-as-one-program-55 = referring (cons "- **Q2** To model markets accurately, resolve economics at large." nil) (cons "- **Q2** (quantitative research, Avik) To model markets accurately, resolve economics at large." nil)
the-firm-as-one-program-56 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-56 = referring (cons "- **Q3** The quant's job is the reduction of uncertainty about unobserved (often future) events." (cons "  Avik: the quant would as soon predict the parking lot population on a given day as a market price; it is not a distinct part of the job. Speaking of quants as dealing with price data alone forms the problem incorrectly." (cons "  - **Q3.1** The problem: given environmental data, forecast subsequent environment states. The environment is the earth, the physical universe, with myriad inseparable activity within it." (cons "  - **Q3.2** Every equity, commodity and future corresponds to physical events in the real world." (cons "  - **Q3.3** Pricing is a byproduct, an observation, of complete world state. [P1]" nil))))) (cons "- **Q3** (quantitative research, Avik) The quant's job is the reduction of uncertainty about unobserved (often future) events." (cons "  Avik: the quant would as soon predict the parking lot population on a given day as a market price; it is not a distinct part of the job. Speaking of quants as dealing with price data alone forms the problem incorrectly." (cons "  - **Q3.1** The problem: given environmental data, forecast subsequent environment states. The environment is the earth, the physical universe, with myriad inseparable activity within it." (cons "  - **Q3.2** Every equity, commodity and future corresponds to physical events in the real world." (cons "  - **Q3.3** Pricing is a byproduct, an observation, of complete world state. [P1: Observation fibers: what a reading warrants, and when a participant is safe to act (hyperactivity v31 §1, §10.4)]" nil)))))
the-firm-as-one-program-57 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-57 = referring (cons "- **Q4** The epistemic basis of prediction: no prior distribution, ever; exact inference over the present." (cons (quoted (cons "  Avik: assuming a prior is pure assumption, not reality, and cannot ground any claim of truth; a uniform prior is a worse sin than a reasoned one. Information " (cons "from tomorrow" (cons " is metaphysically nonsensical: tomorrow is undetermined now. [P1], [N2]" nil)))) (cons "  - **Q4.1** The object of analysis is not a prediction of price, since every action taken influences the world and the price." (cons "  - **Q4.2** The object is exact inference over the present: rationally exposing present information others have not." (cons "  - **Q4.3** We infer and predict the future into existence: when brains are called prediction machines, the prediction is the action; there is no separate action." (cons (quoted (cons "    predict: Latin praedicere, prae " (cons "before" (cons " + dicere " (cons "to say" (cons ", from the root *deyk- " (cons "to show, point out" (cons " (indicate, index, teach). infer: Latin inferre, " (cons "to carry into" (cons "." nil)))))))))) nil)))))) (cons "- **Q4** (quantitative research, Avik) The epistemic basis of prediction: no prior distribution, ever; exact inference over the present." (cons (quoted (cons "  Avik: assuming a prior is pure assumption, not reality, and cannot ground any claim of truth; a uniform prior is a worse sin than a reasoned one. Information " (cons "from tomorrow" (cons " is metaphysically nonsensical: tomorrow is undetermined now. [P1: Observation fibers: what a reading warrants, and when a participant is safe to act (hyperactivity v31 §1, §10.4)], [N2: The bridge to the rationality claim]" nil)))) (cons "  - **Q4.1** The object of analysis is not a prediction of price, since every action taken influences the world and the price." (cons "  - **Q4.2** The object is exact inference over the present: rationally exposing present information others have not." (cons "  - **Q4.3** We infer and predict the future into existence: when brains are called prediction machines, the prediction is the action; there is no separate action." (cons (quoted (cons "    predict: Latin praedicere, prae " (cons "before" (cons " + dicere " (cons "to say" (cons ", from the root *deyk- " (cons "to show, point out" (cons " (indicate, index, teach). infer: Latin inferre, " (cons "to carry into" (cons "." nil)))))))))) nil))))))
the-firm-as-one-program-58 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-58 = referring (cons "- **Q5** Alpha is exposure: present the present information to the market and be paid for the activity the exposure releases in the economy." (cons "  - **Q5.1** The mature market looks like investigative research: never predicting a price, but asking what information the current price reflects, and whether it already reflects the exposure of this information." (cons "  - **Q5.2** The quant's work is fundamentally studying the true underlying value of companies and realizing it: the quant operates over a market ignorant of the true value of things and is tasked with exposing it." (cons "  - **Q5.3** Avik's example: his quantitative analysis that OpenAI and Anthropic go out of business by 2028, from information about the state of the world in November 2026 (his own work) that other quants lack." nil)))) (cons "- **Q5** (quantitative research, Avik) Alpha is exposure: present the present information to the market and be paid for the activity the exposure releases in the economy." (cons "  - **Q5.1** The mature market looks like investigative research: never predicting a price, but asking what information the current price reflects, and whether it already reflects the exposure of this information." (cons "  - **Q5.2** The quant's work is fundamentally studying the true underlying value of companies and realizing it: the quant operates over a market ignorant of the true value of things and is tasked with exposing it." (cons "  - **Q5.3** Avik's example: his quantitative analysis that OpenAI and Anthropic go out of business by 2028, from information about the state of the world in November 2026 (his own work) that other quants lack." nil))))
the-firm-as-one-program-59 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-59 = referring (cons "- **Q6** Quantitative research is research into the quantitative loss of an information system: modelling it purely numerically erases fundamentals. The dollar is a metric of loss." (cons "  - **Q6.1** Economics still relies on mathematically inept models; pure mathematics gives clear derivations (capitalism and communism understood from the elements that compose them)." (cons "  - **Q6.2** The success of this work is indivisible from the end of scalar financial systems, as of national borders and authorities. [S4]" nil))) (cons "- **Q6** (quantitative research, Avik) Quantitative research is research into the quantitative loss of an information system: modelling it purely numerically erases fundamentals. The dollar is a metric of loss." (cons "  - **Q6.1** Economics still relies on mathematically inept models; pure mathematics gives clear derivations (capitalism and communism understood from the elements that compose them)." (cons "  - **Q6.2** The success of this work is indivisible from the end of scalar financial systems, as of national borders and authorities. [S4: What Hayek argued prices must carry becomes directly available, so prices stop being the main way the economy coordinates ([S3], [P9])]" nil)))
the-firm-as-one-program-60 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-60 = referring (cons "- **Q7** Fundamental analysis, and the rationale behind it (will this succeed), can be expressed hyperactively: the actual value and interaction chains composing the world, and rational inference over them." (cons "  - **Q7.1** Deep tech investing: the world is ignorant of a mathematical truth, and here is a company oriented to make money on it. It takes mathematical excellence to the point of norm-rejection." (cons "  - **Q7.2** Correct norm-rejection is the only novelty and value creation." (cons "  - **Q7.3** Forcing the outcome: invest in a set of initiatives, then hand them the construction they need to work perfectly, creating mutual value among them." (cons "  - **Q7.4** Human ignorance of underlying value is fundamental to the problem definition; what humans have yet to discover is the economic value awaiting." (cons "" nil)))))) (cons "- **Q7** (quantitative research, Avik) Fundamental analysis, and the rationale behind it (will this succeed), can be expressed hyperactively: the actual value and interaction chains composing the world, and rational inference over them." (cons "  - **Q7.1** Deep tech investing: the world is ignorant of a mathematical truth, and here is a company oriented to make money on it. It takes mathematical excellence to the point of norm-rejection." (cons "  - **Q7.2** Correct norm-rejection is the only novelty and value creation." (cons "  - **Q7.3** Forcing the outcome: invest in a set of initiatives, then hand them the construction they need to work perfectly, creating mutual value among them." (cons "  - **Q7.4** Human ignorance of underlying value is fundamental to the problem definition; what humans have yet to discover is the economic value awaiting." nil)))))
