the-firm-as-one-program-63 = referring (cons "- **V2** Duplicate compute disappears ([C3])." (cons "  Results already computed somewhere are recognized and reused while their recorded reads still hold." nil)) (cons "- **V2** (value to a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity) Duplicate compute disappears ([C3: Compute and knowledge accumulate instead of being redone ([P8], [P9])])." (cons "  Results already computed somewhere are recognized and reused while their recorded reads still hold." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-64 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-64 = referring (cons "- **V3** Iteration is faster ([C4], [C7])." (cons "  The fast path and new venues move at research speed." nil)) (cons "- **V3** (value to a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity) Iteration is faster ([C4: The fast path is a specialization that carries its proof ([P5], [P7])], [C7: Exchange changes and new venues propagate ([P4], [P10])])." (cons "  The fast path and new venues move at research speed." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-65 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-65 = referring (cons "- **V4** Capital runs closer to its limits ([C5])." (cons "  Capital runs at proven capacity instead of feared capacity." nil)) (cons "- **V4** (value to a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity) Capital runs closer to its limits ([C5: Risk bounds are invariants of the whole composed system ([C1], [P6])])." (cons "  Capital runs at proven capacity instead of feared capacity." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-66 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-66 = referring (cons "- **V5** Catastrophic tail events, Knight Capital-style, are ruled out ([C5], [C12])." (cons "  Knight Capital lost about 440 million dollars in 45 minutes on 1 August 2012 because one of eight servers kept old code behind a repurposed flag. With content identity per server and a rollout proved over every interleaving, that failure cannot be built." nil)) (cons "- **V5** (value to a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity) Catastrophic tail events, Knight Capital-style, are ruled out ([C5: Risk bounds are invariants of the whole composed system ([C1], [P6])], [C12: The provenance of every running byte is known ([P9])])." (cons "  Knight Capital lost about 440 million dollars in 45 minutes on 1 August 2012 because one of eight servers kept old code behind a repurposed flag. With content identity per server and a rollout proved over every interleaving, that failure cannot be built." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-67 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-67 = referring (cons "- **V6** Compliance and fines ([C8])." (cons "  Compliance shrinks to a projection of the running system, and fines approach zero because violations cannot be constructed." nil)) (cons "- **V6** (value to a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity) Compliance and fines ([C8: Audit trails and compliance are queries over retained effect histories ([P8])])." (cons "  Compliance shrinks to a projection of the running system, and fines approach zero because violations cannot be constructed." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-68 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-68 = referring (cons "- **V7** Downtime ([C9])." (cons "  Downtime after incidents drops from days to minutes." nil)) (cons "- **V7** (value to a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity) Downtime ([C9: Debugging restricts the set of runs compatible with what was observed ([P1])])." (cons "  Downtime after incidents drops from days to minutes." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-69 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-69 = referring (cons "- **V8** Data spend ([C6])." (cons "  Data is priced by how much it shrinks the fibers decisions depend on, before it is bought." nil)) (cons "- **V8** (value to a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity) Data spend ([C6: Exact reasoning under partial observation, and the value of information can be computed ([P1])])." (cons "  Data is priced by how much it shrinks the fibers decisions depend on, before it is bought." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-70 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-70 = referring (cons "- **V9** Research capacity becomes a compute budget ([C10])." (cons "  Research capacity stops being a headcount." nil)) (cons "- **V9** (value to a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity) Research capacity becomes a compute budget ([C10: AI researchers at any scale, because their output is checked, not trusted ([P11])])." (cons "  Research capacity stops being a headcount." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-71 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-71 = referring (cons "- **V10** First into every new market ([C7], [C14])." (cons "  The earliest phase of a market has the widest spreads; entering every new market first captures it each time." nil)) (cons "- **V10** (value to a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity) First into every new market ([C7: Exchange changes and new venues propagate ([P4], [P10])], [C14: Exchange semantics are definitions the firm can reason about ([P4])])." (cons "  The earliest phase of a market has the widest spreads; entering every new market first captures it each time." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-72 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-72 = referring (cons "- **V11** Mergers and vendor dependence ([C11])." (cons "  Acquisitions integrate in weeks; vendors are verified instead of trusted." nil)) (cons "- **V11** (value to a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity) Mergers and vendor dependence ([C11: Acquired systems and vendor software come in by equivalence and lifting ([P3], [P4])])." (cons "  Acquisitions integrate in weeks; vendors are verified instead of trusted." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-73 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-73 = referring (cons "- **V12** Key-person risk and onboarding ([C16])." (cons "  Knowledge stops walking out of the door; new hires are productive in days." nil)) (cons "- **V12** (value to a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity) Key-person risk and onboarding ([C16: Knowledge belongs to the firm, not to individuals, and onboarding is a walk ([P2], [P9])])." (cons "  Knowledge stops walking out of the door; new hires are productive in days." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-74 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-74 = referring (cons "- **V13** Internal friction and happiness ([C17])." (cons "  Disagreement resolves on evidence; the work is derived from the science of human happiness." nil)) (cons "- **V13** (value to a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity) Internal friction and happiness ([C17: Disagreements resolve on a presented shared basis ([P1], plus common ground)])." (cons "  Disagreement resolves on evidence; the work is derived from the science of human happiness." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-75 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-75 = referring (cons "- **V14** Proof sold to clients and regulators as a product ([C1], [C8])." (cons "  Brokers that route retail flow to a market maker must show best execution, and the arrangements are under constant scrutiny. A firm that can hand brokers and regulators a proof that each order was handled by stated rules, at a stated price, against stated market conditions, offers something no competitor can, and the trust of clients becomes something established by construction." (cons "" nil))) (cons "- **V14** (value to a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity) Proof sold to clients and regulators as a product ([C1: Prove any provable property of the whole firm ([P2], [P6], [P7])], [C8: Audit trails and compliance are queries over retained effect histories ([P8])])." (cons "  Brokers that route retail flow to a market maker must show best execution, and the arrangements are under constant scrutiny. A firm that can hand brokers and regulators a proof that each order was handled by stated rules, at a stated price, against stated market conditions, offers something no competitor can, and the trust of clients becomes something established by construction." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-76 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-76 = part (cons "## 4. The structural shift" (cons "" nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-77 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-77 = referring (cons "- **S1** The gains multiply instead of adding, which changes the firm's rate of learning (all of layer 3)." (cons "  The lines do not add; they multiply. Faster iteration means more strategies tested, cumulative knowledge means each test builds on all earlier ones, proven risk means more capital behind each, and exact reasoning under uncertainty means better decisions per unit of capital. Artificial researchers multiply all of it again. The result is a firm whose rate of learning is itself rising. Its advantage over competitors is a difference in kind, not a margin." nil)) (cons "- **S1** (the structural shift for a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity) The gains multiply instead of adding, which changes the firm's rate of learning (all of layer 3)." (cons "  The lines do not add; they multiply. Faster iteration means more strategies tested, cumulative knowledge means each test builds on all earlier ones, proven risk means more capital behind each, and exact reasoning under uncertainty means better decisions per unit of capital. Artificial researchers multiply all of it again. The result is a firm whose rate of learning is itself rising. Its advantage over competitors is a difference in kind, not a margin." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-78 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-78 = referring (cons "- **S2** The market concentrates toward the firm that has this ([S1])." (cons "  Electronic trading is close to a zero-sum contest between firms over the same flow, and market share already concentrates toward the firms with the best technology. A discontinuity in technology produces a discontinuity in concentration: the firm that has this takes opportunities first, correctly, at full size, everywhere, and its competitors trade against a counterparty that is better informed and quicker to adapt. That is why a figure of several billion understates it." nil)) (cons "- **S2** (the structural shift for a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity) The market concentrates toward the firm that has this ([S1: The gains multiply instead of adding, which changes the firm's rate of learning (all of layer 3)])." (cons "  Electronic trading is close to a zero-sum contest between firms over the same flow, and market share already concentrates toward the firms with the best technology. A discontinuity in technology produces a discontinuity in concentration: the firm that has this takes opportunities first, correctly, at full size, everywhere, and its competitors trade against a counterparty that is better informed and quicker to adapt. That is why a figure of several billion understates it." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-79 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-79 = referring (cons "- **S3** Prices converge on what is true, so the edge that profits came from shrinks ([S2])." (cons "  Edge in markets is information not yet reflected in prices. As the firm extracts it, prices become correct sooner, and the edge available to everyone shrinks. The firm profits precisely by removing the ignorance that made profit possible. Profit in trading measures collective ignorance, and this system dispels collective ignorance at machine speed." nil)) (cons "- **S3** (the structural shift for a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity) Prices converge on what is true, so the edge that profits came from shrinks ([S2: The market concentrates toward the firm that has this ([S1])])." (cons "  Edge in markets is information not yet reflected in prices. As the firm extracts it, prices become correct sooner, and the edge available to everyone shrinks. The firm profits precisely by removing the ignorance that made profit possible. Profit in trading measures collective ignorance, and this system dispels collective ignorance at machine speed." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-80 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-80 = referring (cons "- **S4** What Hayek argued prices must carry becomes directly available, so prices stop being the main way the economy coordinates ([S3], [P9])." (cons "  Hayek argued in 1945 that no central planner could hold the knowledge dispersed across a society, so prices had to carry it in compressed form. Hyperactivity is not a central planner: it has no canonical state, every participant holds its own, and constructions are exchanged between peers. But the knowledge that prices compress becomes available directly, with its evidence, to every participant. Once that holds, prices stop being the primary carrier of coordination, and an economy built around competing partial knowledge gives way to one built around shared knowledge. The trading firm is where this starts, because no institution has more money riding on the gap between what prices know and what is true. The same mechanism, aimed at knowledge instead of money, is the dispelling of ignorance across the human superorganism: thousands of minds in one firm becoming one reasoning process is the small case of billions of minds doing the same." (cons "" nil))) (cons "- **S4** (the structural shift for a trading firm built as one program in hyperactivity) What Hayek argued prices must carry becomes directly available, so prices stop being the main way the economy coordinates ([S3: Prices converge on what is true, so the edge that profits came from shrinks ([S2])], [P9: Content-addressed, decentralized exchange of code with its proofs (hyperactivity v31 §10.8)])." (cons "  Hayek argued in 1945 that no central planner could hold the knowledge dispersed across a society, so prices had to carry it in compressed form. Hyperactivity is not a central planner: it has no canonical state, every participant holds its own, and constructions are exchanged between peers. But the knowledge that prices compress becomes available directly, with its evidence, to every participant. Once that holds, prices stop being the primary carrier of coordination, and an economy built around competing partial knowledge gives way to one built around shared knowledge. The trading firm is where this starts, because no institution has more money riding on the gap between what prices know and what is true. The same mechanism, aimed at knowledge instead of money, is the dispelling of ignorance across the human superorganism: thousands of minds in one firm becoming one reasoning process is the small case of billions of minds doing the same." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-81 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-81 = part (cons "## Notes" (cons "" nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-82 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-82 = referring (cons "- **N1** Two points carry the most weight." (cons "  C10 is the largest multiplier: checked construction lets AI research scale without trust. S1 is what turns a list of savings into a change in kind. See [C10], [S1]." nil)) (cons "- **N1** (a note on the outline “The Firm as One Program”) Two points carry the most weight." (cons "  C10 (AI researchers at any scale, because their output is checked, not trusted ([P11])) is the largest multiplier: checked construction lets AI research scale without trust. S1 (The gains multiply instead of adding, which changes the firm's rate of learning (all of layer 3)) is what turns a list of savings into a change in kind. See [C10: AI researchers at any scale, because their output is checked, not trusted ([P11])], [S1: The gains multiply instead of adding, which changes the firm's rate of learning (all of layer 3)]." nil))
the-firm-as-one-program-83 : Part
the-firm-as-one-program-83 = referring (cons "- **N2** The bridge to the rationality claim." (cons (quoted (cons "  P1's warrant is the formal form of " (cons "the rational actor cannot be incorrect" (cons ", and that is what C17 runs on. A rational actor concludes P only when it holds a construction of P over every history compatible with what it observed. Where no such construction exists it concludes nothing, so it is never wrong. The language therefore marks exactly what is amenable to rule-based logic: what is derived, what is observed, and what is a stated premise. English could always carry perfect inference for the rational; the language makes that discipline executable and shared. See [P1], [C17]." nil)))) nil)) (cons "- **N2** (a note on the outline “The Firm as One Program”) The bridge to the rationality claim." (cons (quoted (cons "  P1 (Observation fibers: what a reading warrants, and when a participant is safe to act (§1, §10.4))'s warrant is the formal form of " (cons "the rational actor cannot be incorrect" (cons ", and that is what C17 (Disagreements resolve on a presented shared basis ([P1], plus common ground)) runs on. A rational actor concludes P only when it holds a construction of P over every history compatible with what it observed. Where no such construction exists it concludes nothing, so it is never wrong. The language therefore marks exactly what is amenable to rule-based logic: what is derived, what is observed, and what is a stated premise. English could always carry perfect inference for the rational; the language makes that discipline executable and shared. See [P1: Observation fibers: what a reading warrants, and when a participant is safe to act (hyperactivity v31 §1, §10.4)], [C17: Disagreements resolve on a presented shared basis ([P1], plus common ground)]." nil)))) nil))
